RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
August 9, 2010
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne and
Mr. Valdez.  Absent: Mr. Spiker.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City
Treasurer, and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)   Mr. Collins  moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded
by Mr. Pierson. Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on July 26, 2010.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Vouchers Meeting of the Governing Body on August 2, 2010.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Brown  moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Valdez.
Upon inquiry, City Treasurer Barb Dorr and Mayor Kaysen provided information available
concerning a voucher payable to B&B Sewer Service ($180.00), pump out of grease trap at Shadows
Restaurant, Depot Building, and City Engineer Doug Vetter reviewed a voucher payable to Knife
River, ($55.51),  washed rock landscape material at Harmony Meadows for City drainage repair.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
“An Ordinance amending Title 17, Zoning, Chapter 17.08, Zoning Districts Established and
Section 17.08.040 Cheyenne City map of the Cheyenne City Code, by changing the zoning
classification from P Public District to HR-2 High Density-Residential Developing District for
Fincher Block, a replat of Lots 1-8, Block 193, and vacated 16-foot alley contained within said
Block 193, Original City, Cheyenne, Wyoming (located between Bradley and Morrie Avenues, and
E. 22nd and 23rd Streets).”  Reporting for Public Services Committee, Ms. Ash moved to approve
on third and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of
the governing body present. (#3902)
“An Ordinance amending Title 17, Zoning, Chapter 17.08, Zoning Districts Established and
Section 17.08.040 Cheyenne city map of the Cheyenne City Code, by changing the zoning
classification from P-Public, MR-1-Medium Residential Established and LI-Light Industrial
Districts to LI-Light Industrial District for BOPU Subdivision, a replat of portions of Blocks 98, 99,
and 151; all of Blocks 149 and 150; and vacated streets and alleyways, Original City, Cheyenne,
Wyoming (located at the northwest corner of the intersection of Snyder Avenue and W. 24th
Street).”  Ms. Ash moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Motion
```

