```text
[CA]
Contract Modification #3 to Contract  #5477 between the City of Cheyenne and Recco, Inc.
d/b/a Five-R Co. to substitute 277 volt heaters with 208 volt heaters to accommodate existing
electrical system at the City Transfer Station (State Land and Investment Board funds) -- referred
to Finance Committee.

[CA]
Amendment Number One to Cooperative Agreement #5512 between the City of Cheyenne
and Wyoming Department of Transportation for Cheyenne Marginal-Vandehei Interchange (2007-
2010 1% Sales Tax) -- referred to Finance Committee.
[CA]
Consideration of #Bid R-2-11 for furnishing one new Motor Grader for the City of Cheyenne
Street & Alley Division from Honnen Equipment, Casper, WY.  Motion (per Consent Agenda)
carried.
Appointment of Donald Threewit to the Historic Preservation Board.  Mr. Collins moved to
approve, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing
body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote (Mayoral appointment).
Announcement was made of the appointment of Lorna Sanders to the Housing & Community
Development Advisory Council, to be confirmed August 23, 2010.
Under other City business:
Steven Martinez stated he had recently reapplied for a Body Artist business permit and
requested information regarding the review status of the application. Police Chief Brian Kozak
advised he had completed his review and his recommendation would be to approve. Upon request
by Mr. Martinez as to whether there was any way to “fast track” the remaining application review
process, Mayor Kaysen and City Clerk Carol Intlekofer provided information on the application
processing procedure once Chief Kozak’s written recommendation has been received in the City
Clerk’s office.
Pachomio Sandoval requested information regarding placement of political and other types
of signs in the public right-of-way.  Lisa Pafford, Building and Development Office, advised
political and other signs must be located on private property, not in the public right-of-way, and that
set back distances vary throughout the City depending on property lines, and street width and area
dedicated to the public.  Comment was made on enforcement measures involving signs in the public
right-of-way.
It was noted a fund raiser (Mad Hatter Tea Party) open to the public will be held Sunday
afternoon, August 15, 2010 at the Paul Smith Children’s Village.
Appreciation was expressed to the Police Department for its graffiti removal program and
it was noted that donations are being accepted to assist with program expenses.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, Mayor Kaysen
adjourned the meeting at 6:22 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
```

